sures, e.g. [0.328406186, 5.692597307] for three cubes. G1A: SU(3) on two adjacent plaquettes, gap >= 154/39 at coupling 1/2. G1D: SU(3) on one cube. All 28 Umeno records are SU(3); 0 concern a finite gauge group (MEASURED by A-hunter, Zenodo API). Mariani 2023: D4 on 2x2 (dim 8960), numerical diagonalization, no certified bounds. Mariani 2024: D4 and Q8 on 2x2 and 2x3 (dim up to 536,576), sparse eigensolver, no error bounds. Pradhan 2023: D4 2x2 ED, uncertified. Popov et al.: D3 = S3 and D4 ladders with 4 to 60 rungs, DMRG, fit errors only, a different electric operator (alpha_0=0, alpha_tau=1, alpha_p=10). Flores-Calderon et al.: D(S3) quantum double, sign-free QMC, no gaps. Caspar et al.: S3 in a doubled Chern-Simons-Yang-Mills Hamiltonian, exact single-cross electric spectrum only. Ours rests on a computational Perron complement floor (#131 plus its lift), not an analytic bound, so it is conditional|contrary=Umeno's series (2026-10-12 to 2026-11-05) gives certified two-sided gap and cluster enclosures for interacting non-Abelian lattice gauge Hamiltonians 2 to 4 weeks before #136 (merged 2026-11-08); it cuts against novelty of the technique and of the kind of result, not of this model's theorem; the physical dimension 2,177,317,873 is prior (Mariani et al. eq. (3.12): 6^12+3^12+2^12; OEIS A074528) and is not a candidate; Bravyi, Hastings and Michalakis 2010, J. Math. Phys. 51, 093512, arXiv:1001.0344 (abstract only) give the qualitative expectation of a low cluster with small splitting under small perturbations of commuting-projector models, with no numbers and a small-epsilon hypothesis not shown at r=9; Caspar et al. 2016 show finite-S3 Hamiltonian spectra predate this work (different Hamiltonian); Novickis, Zenodo 20547250 (2026-06-04), claims a Lean-4 machine-checked U(1) strong-coupling gap (record page only, UNVERIFIED, not peer reviewed)|unverified=Popov v2; unread later parts of the Mariani 2023 and 2024 and Flores-Calderon HTML; Umeno G1A v2 body, G1C 2