PRIORITY|candidate=A2-technique #136 eight-flat Feshbach/Schur sandwich: K_z=W(bH-aI), S(z)=C-F^T A^-1 F, arbitrary integer trial X_int, residual R=LF-AX_int, UPPER=U, LOWER=6 gamma_num U - 10^6 G, n_-(UPPER) <= N_full(z) <= n_-(LOWER) by integer Bareiss (FINITE_S3_3X4_R9_FIRST_GAP_20261108.md lines 34-60)|class=PRIOR|label=PRIORITY_UNVERIFIED|closest=S. Boyd and L. Vandenberghe, Convex Optimization, Cambridge Univ. Press 2004, App. A.5.5 eq. (A.14) ('The Schur complement arises when you minimize a quadratic form over some of the variables ... the optimal value is inf_u [u;v]^T X [u;v] = v^T S v'), VERIFIED (primary PDF); E.V. Haynsworth 1968, Determination of the inertia of a partitioned Hermitian matrix, Linear Algebra Appl. 1, 73-81, UNVERIFIED primary (inertia additivity restated on Wikipedia 'Schur complement', opened; the repo cites Haynsworth); Courant-Fischer min-max and Lowner-order reversal of the inverse, classical, UNVERIFIED primaries; Umeno 23313816 Thm 5.1 and Sec. 1.1, VERIFIED; Umeno 23641690 Thm 3.1 and Cor. 3.2, VERIFIED; Umeno, Certified Lehmann-Maehly Lower Bounds for the One-Cube SU(3) Lattice Gauge Hamiltonian, Zenodo 2026-10-30, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23789573, VERIFIED; Dusson, Sigal and Stamm, The Feshbach-Schur map and perturbation theory, arXiv:2105.02058 Thm 1.2, VERIFIED, and Math. Comp. 92 (2023) 217-249, doi:10.1090/mcom/3774, arXiv:2008.10871, VERIFIED abstract; Behnke, Mertins, Plum and Wieners 2000, Proc. R. Soc. Lond. A 456, 2717-2730, Thm 2.1 (Lehmann-Goerisch), VERIFIED as restated in Vejchodsky arXiv:1801.02561, primary UNVERIFIED; Bach, Frohlich and Sigal 1998, Adv. Math. 137, 205-298, doi:10.1006/aima.1998.1733, UNVERIFIED; Lehmann 1949/1950 ZAMM 29 and 30, Behnke-Goerisch 1994, Temple 1928, Kato 1949, Lowdin 1965 Phys. Rev. 139 A357, Bareiss 1968 Math. Comp. 22, UNVERIFIED citations|comparison=With M=[[C,F^T],[F,A]], A>0 and trial vector (Lv,-Xv): (i) (A.14) gives form(Lv,-Xv) >= inf_y form(Lv,y) = L^2 v^T S v, so UPPER >= L^2 S; (ii) the excess of a quadratic over its minimum is exact, form(Lv,-Xv) - L^2 v^T S v = r^T A^-1 r with r=Rv, which is #136's 'L^2 S(z) = U - R^T A^-1 R'; (iii) A >= gamma W_Q implies A^-1 <= W_Q^-1/gamma (Lowner-order reversal), giving LOWER up to the positive scalings 6 gamma_num and 10^6; (iv) Courant-Fischer gives n_-(UPPER) <= n_-(S) <= n_-(LOWER), and Haynsworth gives N_full(z) = n_-(S(z)) when A(z)>0. The script docstring itself calls step (iii) 'the exact Feshbach identity'. Umeno Thm 5.1 is the X=0 special case (F_d(t) = A - tI - B*B/(d-t)) with an analytic complement floor. Steps (i)-(iv) were re-derived by hand in the report step (not run). What is left (an 8x8 test for a 2.18e9-dimensional space through an arbitrary X on a ball; integer-only Bareiss; a computational Perron floor) is implementation|contrary=Against the PRIOR class (preserved, from A-hunter): the scope's PRIOR means 'an earlier theorem already implies the result', and here the implication is a four-step composition of classical statements, not one theorem; no opened source states the composed two-sided sandwich for arbitrary X as one result; the verified-numerics monographs (Nakao-Plum-Watanabe 2019, Rump 2010, Liu 2024, Barrenechea-Boulton-Boussaid 2017 Numer. Math. 135) were not opened; an adjudicator may keep lane A2's PARTIALLY_PRIOR. Against originality: Umeno G1A Sec. 1.1, 'The Schur-complement principle and its use in certified spectral approximation are also established methods' and 'neither a gauge-invariant basis nor a two-plaquette calculation alone establishes novelty'; Umeno G1B Sec. 1, 'Schur and Feshbach reductions, min-max bounds, and verified eigenvalue enclosures are standard tools' and 'Temple-type bounds use a residual together with prior spectral separation'; Lehmann-Goerisch needs only an a priori lower bound on one higher eigenvalue, so an E9 bound with exactly computable second moments is sufficient pre-information for Lehmann-Maehly lower bounds on E1..E8 (Umeno 23789573 does this for one SU(3) cube); the README sentence 'an E9 lower bound alone would not justify the resolvent' is true of the chosen Schur method, not a necessity of certification (flagged for the adjudicator, not rewritten); symveig arXiv:2606.16217 and CERTIFY-ED arXiv:2605.11787 (abstracts) show certified exact diagonalization is an established direction (floating-point methods); Lemm, Sandvik and Wang 2020, PRL 124, 177204, arXiv:1910.11810 (abstract) is model-specific computer-assisted gap precedent by a different, numerical method|unverified=Haynsworth, Courant-Fischer, Lowner, Lehmann, Goerisch, Behnke-Goerisch, Behnke-Mertins-Plum-Wieners, Temple, Kato, Lowdin and Bareiss primaries not opened; verified-numerics monographs not searched; Umeno G1B's 20-layer L1 test not compared in detail with the X-based residual; the M-matrix test-vector lemma behind a computational floor seen only as a search snippet (De Groen 1980 CWI report; J. Inequal. Appl. 2024); Umeno authorship verified only from records and PDF headers|novelty_kind=none at the level of mathematics (classical identities composed); the implementation choices are engineering|importance=method-level; the 8x8 reduction for a 2.18e9-state space is practically significant; a PRIOR label for the lemma does not reduce the model result A2|json=0
